*5 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*5 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage, like most other [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]]-focused ones, heavily relies on luck. This is, of course, unless you use [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] with a 100% [[Critical Hit|Critical]] chance. If you have any [[METAL BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|METAL BUSTERS]] or [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan]], make sure to use them. Also, bring a wave-attacking cat ([[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] is ideal) or a long-ranged one for the Mooths, add [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress]] and [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Major Space Cat]] as Critters (Don't use most other non-uber Critters as they tend to have short range. [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]] or her variants may work, but not very well.) and add a bunch more Critters. If you can throw in a useful [[Cat Combo|Combo]] ([[Gross!!! (Combo)|Gross!!!]], [[Spearfight (Combo)|Spearfight]], [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]], or any "[[Worker Cat]] Start Level Up" Combos) feel free to try.

One useful tip is to abuse the "boss" mechanic by facing the Sir Metal Seal at their base. That way, you can more easily stack shorter ranged critters as the Sir Metal Seal will be unable to be knocked back behind its base, thus preventing your units from pushing into the Mooth's range.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any Uber that has [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal abilities]] and/or can do [[Critical Hit]]s with a decent chance, will be good here. Listed below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]]: Has a chance to perform a [[Critical Hit]] that can instantly dispatch of the Sir Metal Seal.
*[[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Princess Kaguya]]: Has a fast attack rate and good Crowd-Controlling abilities.
*[[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Marauder Cat]]: Just like most other stages full of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, Marauder Cat make this stage a joke as long as he is in his Evolved Form or higher.
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]: An even better option, can destroy most if not all of the Metal enemies in this stage with his powerful, [[Long Distance]] strikes.
*[[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sakura Sonic]]: Great [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Control]] for all the Metal enemies here and has a chance to do a [[Critical Hit]].
*[[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Wrathful Poseidon]]: Can Freeze Sir Metal Seal for a decent amount of time, allowing your Critters to freely chip away at him.
*[[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]]: If you are fortunate to have unlocked her, she completely trivializes this stage by dishing out decently strong Crits while also being extremely tanky against Metal.
*[[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Agent Staal]]: Also trivializes this stage. His blazing fast attack speed can kill the Metal Doges without even needing to Crit, and his constant Slows and Crits stop the Metal enemies from advancing.
*[[Mech Patrol Axel (Uber Rare Cat)|Mech Patrol Axel]]: good cc unit with a conjure that uses 40% metal killer, both forms are good, so use the one you prefer.

==Trivia==
*Like most [[Singularityville]] stages, Blockchain Twilight has a technology-related name. A [[wikipedia:Blockchain|blockchain]] is a digital ledger that records transactions and ownership of assets in a series of "blocks", each linked to the last such that they cannot be retroactively changed in any way.

